    end
end
disp(uniqueWords);
```
In this modified code, we use the `memmap` function to map the text files into memory, and the `parfor` loop to parallelize the computation. The `parfor` loop iterates over each word in `words1`, and checks if it appears in `words2`. If it doesn't, it adds it to the `uniqueWords` array. Finally, the `disp` function prints the unique words.

