3. Click on the "Settings" tab and copy the "Domain" and "Client ID" values.
4. In each of your React apps, install the `@auth0/auth0-react` package by running `npm install @auth0/auth0-react`.
5. In each app, create a new file called `auth0.js` and import the necessary packages:
```javascript
import { Auth0Provider, useAuth0 } from '@auth0/auth0-react';
```
6. In the `auth0.js` file, create a new instance of the `Auth0Provider` and pass in the domain and client ID values you copied earlier:
```javascript
const auth0Provider = new Auth0Provider(
  'your_domain',
  'your_client_id'
);
```
7. Wrap your entire app in the `Auth0Provider` component:
```javascript
function App() {
  return (
    <Auth0Provider {...auth0Provider}>
      {/* Your app content goes here */}
    </Auth0Provider>
  );
}

export default App;
```
